<!-- Text-Based Step-by-Step Workflow Section -->
<section>
    <h2>Step-by-Step Execution Flow</h2>
    <p>The sequence of operations processed from top to bottom when an HTTP request hits the API:</p>

    <pre style="background-color: #f8f9fa; padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: 6px; border: 1px solid #e9ecef; font-family: monospace; font-size: 0.9rem; overflow-x: auto; line-height: 1.5;">
[ Blazor Client (Blazor Client) ]
           │
           │ Sends HTTP GET Request with "X-API-KEY" Header
           │ client.DefaultRequestHeaders.Add("X-API-KEY", "SuperSecretApiKey-12345")
           ▼
[ ASP.NET Core API Pipeline (DemoApi) ]
           │
           │ Incoming request reaches middleware layer
           ▼
[ ApiKeyMiddleware ]
           │
           ├──► Step 1: Checks if request path is "/swagger" (Bypasses if true)
           │
           ├──► Step 2: Attempts to extract "X-API-KEY" from request headers
           │            ├── If missing ──► Returns [ 401 Unauthorized ] (Stop)
           │            └── If found   ──► Proceeds
           │
           └──► Step 3: Compares extracted key with configuration key (appsettings.json)
                        ├── If invalid ──► Returns [ 401 Unauthorized ] (Stop)
                        └── If valid   ──► Calls _next() to continue pipeline
           │
           ▼
[ Controller & Action: WeatherForecastController ]
           │
           │ Executes business logic securely
           ▼
[ Data Generation / Return Response ]
           │
           │ Returns [ 200 OK ] with requested data payload
           ▼
[ Blazor Client receives the Weather Data ]
    </pre>
</section>